within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.B_BloodAndBloodFormingOrgans.B01A_AntithromboticAgents.B01AE07_DabigatranEtexilate;
model DabigatranEtexilate_Liesenfeld2006_PD_aptt
  "emax exposure-response sweep — Liesenfeld_2006 :: aPTT (activated partial thromboplastin time)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 33.4,      // [s; s × 1]
    Emax = 26.9,  // [s; s × 1]
    EC50 = 9.47e-05,  // [kg/m3; ng ml(-1) × 1e-06]
    gamma = 1,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 ng ml(-1) per second
  // defaulted: gamma
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 950, Interval = 1.9),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>DabigatranEtexilate_Liesenfeld2006_PD_aptt</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Liesenfeld KH et al., <i>British journal of clinical pharmacology 62(5):527–537</i> 2006 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-2125.2006.02667.x\">doi:10.1111/j.1365-2125.2006.02667.x</a>) — activated partial thromboplastin time [s] against dabigatran ng ml(-1) — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       33.4 s        drug-free response (baseline) (baseline aPTT, Q324)
  Emax  =       26.9 s        maximal effect term (E(max), Q320)
  EC50  =       94.7 ng ml(-1) exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC(50), Q321)
  gamma = (library default) Hill coefficient</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one ng ml(-1) of dabigatran per second of simulated time (exposure is in kg/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 33.4   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (94.7 ng ml(-1))  response 46.85
  exposure -> infinity  response 60.3</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Liesenfeld_2006: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: accepted with caveats</li></ul></body></html>"));
end DabigatranEtexilate_Liesenfeld2006_PD_aptt;
